This patch fixes RISC-V model exports by adding the missing SetValid() call.
Apply to IMDb repository models: Pico, Piccolo, Rocket, Nibbler.

Root cause: These models were created before SetValid() became mandatory for JSON export.
Fix: Add model.SetValid(BoolConst(true)) at the beginning of addInstructions().

================================================================================
PATCH 1/4: Pico
================================================================================
File: IMDb/IMDb_Cores/ILA_Pico/RISC-V-Spec/src/riscvIla.cc
Line: 122-123

--- a/IMDb/IMDb_Cores/ILA_Pico/RISC-V-Spec/src/riscvIla.cc
+++ b/IMDb/IMDb_Cores/ILA_Pico/RISC-V-Spec/src/riscvIla.cc
@@ -121,6 +121,10 @@

 void riscvILA_user::addInstructions() {
+  // PATCH: Set valid expression (required for JSON export)
+  // This was added to ILAng after Pico was created
+  model.SetValid(BoolConst(true));
+
   // ------------------------- Instruction: BRANCH
   // ------------------------------ //
   {

